[[File:lockeditemroomdoor.png]][[File:itemroomdoor.png]]

{{dlc+|r}}[[File:Devil Treasure Room door locked.png]][[File:Devil Treasure Room door.png]] with {{t|Devil's Crown}}{{dlc-}}

A '''Treasure Room''', or Item Room, is a room that contains items from the {{ip|Treasure Room|text=Treasure Room item pool}}. They appear in [[chapters]] 1, 2, and 3 (and 4 if Isaac holds {{t|Bloody Crown}}, 5 with {{t|Holy Crown}} or {{t|Wicked Crown}}). Two also appear in the {{s|???}}. A Treasure Room can be identified by the gold edges of the door. When the current floor is under the effect of {{Cu|Labyrinth}}, making a floor an XL floor, there will be two Treasure Rooms on the floor instead of one.

Treasure Rooms on the first floor of any run do not require a key to open, even under the effect of Curse of the Labyrinth. Treasure Rooms never border more than a single regular room, but there may be a {{R|Secret Room}} adjacent to it.

{{dlc|a}} In [[Greed Mode]], Treasure Rooms appear in Chapters 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5, and are always locked. Silver Treasure Rooms appear next to these rooms, they give items from the {{ip|Boss|text=Boss Room item pool}} but are always unlocked.

== Variations ==
* {{dlc|a}} There is a rare chance that a Treasure Room might contain two items, only one of which can be taken.
** {{dlc|a+}} Occasionally, both items can be taken. In this case, the treasure room will have a unique layout with 8 "special" obstacles ([[Urn]]s in {{s|Basement}}, [[Mushroom]]s in {{s|Caves}} and so on). 
** {{T|Golden Horse Shoe}} will increase the chance for a Treasure Room to become a double Treasure Room, and {{I|More Options}} will cause every Treasure Room to become a double Treasure Room.
** {{dlc|r}} If the Treasure Room was unexplored, {{i|Tarot Cloth|n}} + {{p|XVII - The Stars}} will make the Treasure Room a double Treasure Room.
** {{dlc+|r}} Treasure Rooms in {{s|Downpour}}, {{s|Dross}}, {{s|Mines}}, {{s|Ashpit}}, {{s|Mausoleum}}, {{s|Gehenna}}, and {{s|Corpse}} will always contain two items. One item will be hidden with a non-removable {{Cu|Blind}} effect.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc|r}} If a Treasure Room on the alt path spawns with an extra item, it will have three items. One can be taken freely while the other two are still a choice. There is no visual indication which is which, although one of the choice items is still hidden.
*** {{t|Broken Glasses}} have a chance to add a hidden item choice to regular Treasure Rooms, or reveal the hidden choice in alt Treasure Rooms.
* {{dlc+|a}} Treasure Rooms may contain a {{M|Shop Restock Machine}}, allowing Isaac to re-roll offered items if he has coins or bombs.{{dlc-}}
** {{t|Pay to Win}} guarantees a Shop Restock Machine in newly generated Treasure Rooms.
* {{dlc|a+nr}} 2-3 {{E|Greed Gaper|x}}s may appear in some rooms.
* {{dlc|r}} 1-3 {{E|Bulb|x}}s may appear in some rooms.
* {{dlc|r}} Some themed enemies from their respective floors may appear in some alt path Treasure Rooms.
* Treasure Rooms have a few very rare layouts that do not spawn items. Instead, they spawn:
** {{dlc|a+}} {{E|Poop}} surrounded by a [[trinket]], five pickups, and {{e|Attack Fly|text=Attack Flies}}.
** {{dlc|a+}} A trinket surrounded by eight pickups.
** {{dlc+|r}} ({{s|Downpour}} only) A trinket surrounded by four {{E|Blue Fire Place}}s, with two pairs of [[Pills]], [[Card]]s or [[Rune]]s.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} ({{s|Mines}} only) Eight various pickups in the middle of the room, with additional pickups surrounded by rocks and a fireplace at each corner.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} ({{s|Ashpit}} only) A {{M|Key Master}}, with [[key]]s surrounded by [[spiked rock]]s on the top left and bottom right of the room.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} ({{s|Mausoleum}} and {{s|Gehenna}} only) [[Spikes]] surrounded by a trinket, two [[Golden Chest]]s, one [[Stone Chest]], a trinket, and a random heart, bomb, key and pill.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} ({{s|Corpse}} only) A {{M|Rotten Beggar}} and a random coin at each room corner.{{dlc-}}

